BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20261020-google-public-sector-summit@techpolicyhub.umd.edu
DTSTAMP:20261020T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Google Public Sector Summit
DESCRIPTION:The Google Public Sector Summit bridges the gap between ambitious innovation and secure\, scaled execution. Tailored for leaders\, creators\, coders\, and builders\, the event focuses on moving organizations beyond AI pilots and experimentation into fully deployed\, mission-ready realities. By leveraging a secure\, integrated AI stack—encompassing everything from planet-scale infrastructure to leading models and agentic platforms—attendees will learn how to safely navigate and thrive in the emerging agentic era.
CATEGORIES:External
URL:https://events.govexec.com/google-public-sector-summit/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20261111-cybersecurity-in-the-age-of-agents@techpolicyhub.umd.edu
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Cybersecurity in the age of Agents
LOCATION:Virtual
DESCRIPTION:​AI agents are changing the cybersecurity playbook. How might they shift the balance between attackers and defenders\, and what will that mean for the institutions and communities they target?  ​Join the University of Maryland’s Tech Policy Hub for Cybersecurity in the Age of AI\, a virtual conversation hosted by Dr. Ido Sivan-Sevilla\, featuring:  ​Dr. Charlie Harry\, a UMD cybersecurity researcher and director of the Center for Governance of Technology and Systems\, whose experience includes a 14-year career at the National Security Agency.  ​Netta Squires\, an attorney\, cybersecurity and emergency management expert\, and founder of Open District Solutions\, who has led statewide cybersecurity initiatives in Maryland.  ​This installment of the Tech Policy Hub Speaker Series will explore how AI agents are reshaping cyberattacks and defense\, what these changes mean for organizations with limited resources\, and how policy can help communities prepare. Bring your questions for a discussion connecting technical developments with the practical challenges of protecting people\, systems\, and public infrastructure.
CATEGORIES:Speaker Series
URL:https://luma.com/gspdecq1
END:VEVENT
